 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 505769,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Change <span data-math=\"46.113 \\times {10^8}\">46.113 \\times {10^8}</span> by moving the decimal four places to the left.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"46.113 \\times {10^8}\"></span></p>\n<p>When you move the decimal point four places to the left, 46.113 becomes</p>\n<p>0.0046113, or <span data-math=\"4.6113 \\times {10^{ - 4}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>To keep the number the same, you need to multiply by 10<sup>4</sup>. Increase the exponent by 4 to make up for moving the decimal place four places to the left.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"46.113 \\times {10^8} = 0.0046113 \\times {10^{12}}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"0.0046113 \\times {10^{12}}\">0.0046113 \\times {10^{12}}</span>"
    }
   ],
